.Dd September 18, 2026
.Dt RECLAIMSTAT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm reclaimstat
.Nd show what each capability provider is managing
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints, for each capability provider that runs the container-model reconcile
.Pq Xr capsule 8 , docs/book/src/plane/containers-and-storage.md ,
the set of installed bundles whose resources it currently holds and the result
of its most recent reconcile pass.
.Pp
Each provider records this after every pass to
.Pa /var/run/reclaim/ Ns Aq Ar provider
through
.Xr libcapreclaim 3 ;
.Nm
reads those records rather than querying the providers.
The crypto, filesystem, module-extension and jail brokers write their records
here.
A provider that enters capability mode before it can open the directory
.Pq the log broker, which is itself the log store; the Bluetooth broker
keeps its reconcile record in its own container instead and is not listed here.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl a
Also list each provider's orphans: resources whose bundle is gone but which
are still within the reconcile's grace window and have not yet been reaped.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /var/run/reclaim/*" -compact
.It Pa /var/run/reclaim/*
One record per provider, named for the provider, rewritten each reconcile pass.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr capsule 8 ,
.Xr switchboard 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
appeared in
.Fx 16.0
with the capability container model.
